Adapt HandBrake to the 26.04 archive's library versions.

HandBrake 1.11.2 is developed against the exact library snapshots in its
contrib tree: FFmpeg 8.0.2 with HandBrake's patches, SVT-AV1 4.1.0 and an
x265 snapshot carrying HandBrake's ambient-viewing patch. The archive ships
FFmpeg 8.0.1, SVT-AV1 2.3.0 and stock x265 4.1, so three call sites need
adjusting. This is the same kind of adaptation Ubuntu's own handbrake package
needs.

  - libhb/decavcodec.c: FFmpeg 8.0.1 has no
    AV_FRAME_DATA_DOVI_RPU_BUFFER_T35 side-data type (HandBrake's contrib
    FFmpeg adds it). Keep the standard AV_FRAME_DATA_DOVI_RPU_BUFFER path.
  - libhb/encsvtav1.c: SVT-AV1 2.3.0 takes an extra application-data
    argument in svt_av1_enc_init_handle() and has no
    extended_crf_qindex_offset field in EbSvtAv1EncConfiguration, so the
    fractional part of the CRF value cannot be passed to the encoder. Drop
    the corresponding Dolby Vision T35 branch as well (see above).
  - libhb/encx265.c: the ambientIlluminance/ambientLightX/ambientLightY and
    bEmitAmbientViewingEnvironment fields come from HandBrake's contrib x265
    patches, not from stock x265 4.1. The GUI does not offer ambient viewing
    metadata.

--- a/libhb/decavcodec.c
+++ b/libhb/decavcodec.c
@@ -1309,12 +1309,6 @@
             int type = AV_FRAME_DATA_DOVI_RPU_BUFFER;
             sd = av_frame_get_side_data(pv->frame, type);
 
-            if (sd == NULL)
-            {
-                type = AV_FRAME_DATA_DOVI_RPU_BUFFER_T35;
-                sd = av_frame_get_side_data(pv->frame, type);
-            }
-
             if (sd != NULL && sd->size > 0)
             {
                 hb_data_t *rpu = hb_data_init(sd->size);
